From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: a local server's launcher may leave before the class is registered

COM starts the program a class's LocalServer32 names and waits for the class
to be registered -- and gave up as soon as that program exited. Omaha's
BraveUpdateOnDemand.exe (GoogleUpdateOnDemand.exe and the like) only starts
"BraveUpdate.exe /ondemand", which registers the class, and exits: every
activation of its Process Launcher failed ("no class object ... could be
created"), so Brave's installer never opened the browser it had installed.
A program that exits successfully now leaves COM waiting for the class, up
to the usual 30 seconds; one that fails still fails at once.
---
--- a/dlls/combase/rpc.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/rpc.c
@@ -670,9 +670,24 @@
         {
             if (SUCCEEDED(CoWaitForMultipleHandles(0, 1000, (process != 0), &process, &index)) && process && !index)
             {
-                WARN("Server for %s failed to start.\n", debugstr_guid(rclsid));
+                DWORD code = 1;
+
+                /* A program that starts the real server and leaves, as
+                 * Omaha's ...UpdateOnDemand.exe does, exits successfully:
+                 * the class is registered later, by its child, so keep
+                 * waiting for that. A server that failed fails now. */
+                GetExitCodeProcess(process, &code);
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_LAUNCHEREXIT
+                code = 1;
+#endif
                 CloseHandle(process);
-                return E_NOINTERFACE;
+                process = 0;
+                if (code)
+                {
+                    WARN("Server for %s failed to start.\n", debugstr_guid(rclsid));
+                    return E_NOINTERFACE;
+                }
+                TRACE("Server for %s left; waiting for what it started.\n", debugstr_guid(rclsid));
             }
         } while (GetTickCount() - start_ticks < 1000);
 
